description: Rules for this GLPI plugin ({{name}}, key {{key}}, {{glpiLabel}})
globs: ["**/*.php", "setup.php", "hook.php"]
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/glpi-rules.md` before changing PHP. The short version:

- Classes live in `src/` as `GlpiPlugin\{{Key}}\Name`; tables are `glpi_plugin_{{key}}_*`; the right is `plugin_{{key}}`;
  settings are in `glpi_configs` context `plugin:{{key}}`; static files only under `public/`.
- Pages: `include('../../../inc/includes.php');`, `Ui::need(<right>)`, POST handling that ends in
  `Html::redirect(Ui::url('page'))`, then `Ui::header()` … `Ui::footer()`. Form action is `Ui::url('page')`, never
  `$_SERVER['PHP_SELF']`. Put `Ui::csrf()` in forms and never call `Session::checkCSRF()`.
- `Html::redirect()` throws: do not catch `\Throwable` around it.
- Overrides keep GLPI's exact signatures (`canView(): bool`, `getTabNameForItem(CommonGLPI $item, $withtemplate = 0)`,
  `showForm($ID, array $options = [])`). Never declare `public static $rightname`; use `Profile::has()`.
- `hook.php` is additive: guard with `tableExists()` / `fieldExists()`, add missing rights and settings only, gate
  one-time migrations on `$previous`. Never rewrite existing rows on update.
- SQL via `$DB->request([...])`, `insert()`, `update()`, `delete()`, `doQuery()`. Escape output with `Ui::e()`.
  Strings through `__('…', '{{key}}')`.
- Multi-select dropdowns: selected ids in `'value'`. Checkboxes: hidden `0` input first.
- Ship: raise `PLUGIN_{{KEY}}_VERSION`, update `CHANGELOG.md`, run `bash tests/lint.sh <glpi root>`, render each
  changed page once.
